{
  "name": "Understanding Your Roof's Remaining Useful Life",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1: Get Past Age Alone - While a typical new roof might last around 20 years, factors like material quality, installation expertise, and even your home's design significantly impact that. Don't assume a roof's nominal manufacturer life is a guarantee; we look at the actual condition, not just the sticker.",
      "text": "Step 1: Get Past Age Alone - While a typical new roof might last around 20 years, factors like material quality, installation expertise, and even your home's design significantly impact that. Don't assume a roof's nominal manufacturer life is a guarantee; we look at the actual condition, not just the sticker.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 2: Look Beyond the Surface - It's easy to focus on what you can see, but neglecting flashings, drainage, or potential concealed moisture is a common mistake. A professional assessment digs deeper, checking for issues that aren't visible from the ground, especially in areas prone to pooling water or hidden damage.",
      "text": "Step 2: Look Beyond the Surface - It's easy to focus on what you can see, but neglecting flashings, drainage, or potential concealed moisture is a common mistake. A professional assessment digs deeper, checking for issues that aren't visible from the ground, especially in areas prone to pooling water or hidden damage.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 2
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 3: Consider Your Climate's Impact - Texas roofs endure intense sun, wind, and hail. These environmental factors can accelerate wear and tear, meaning a roof in a mild climate might last longer than an identical roof here. We consider local weather patterns in our assessments.",
      "text": "Step 3: Consider Your Climate's Impact - Texas roofs endure intense sun, wind, and hail. These environmental factors can accelerate wear and tear, meaning a roof in a mild climate might last longer than an identical roof here. We consider local weather patterns in our assessments.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 3
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 4: Review Installation and Maintenance History - How was your roof installed? Has it been regularly maintained? These details are crucial. A well-installed roof with consistent care will generally outperform one that wasn't, even if they're the same age and material.",
      "text": "Step 4: Review Installation and Maintenance History - How was your roof installed? Has it been regularly maintained? These details are crucial. A well-installed roof with consistent care will generally outperform one that wasn't, even if they're the same age and material.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 4
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 5: Don't Just Patch, Assess the System - A temporary repair might fix a leak, but it doesn't always address broader deterioration. We help you understand if a repair is truly the best long-term solution or if it's time to consider a more comprehensive approach to protect your home.",
      "text": "Thinking about these elements helps us provide an honest recommendation, so you can make a confident decision. Reach out to Discounted Roofing Co. for a detailed assessment tailored to your roof.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 5
    }
  ],
